      <div type="clause" n="1.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 1.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="46" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa to hwæðrum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="48" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.48"/> þissa genied sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="49" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.49"/> on woh, oððe to hlafordsearwe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="50" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.50"/> oððe to ængum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="51" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.51"/> unryhtum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="52" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.52"/> fultume, þæt is þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> ryhtre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="52" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.52"/> to áleoganne þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> to gelæstanne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="46" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa to hwæðerum þisra genyd sy on woh, oþþe to hlafordsearwe oððe to ænigum unrihtum fultume, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þonne rihtre is to aleogenne þonne to gelæstanne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="47" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis tamen ad alterutrum cogatur iniuste, uel ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.21"/> proditionem domini uel iniustum aliquod adiutorium, rectius est hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.14"/> ementiri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.oe.22"/> quam implere.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="62" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif hwa to hwæðrum þissa genied sie<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Af_1-1.attnote.fn.10"/> on woh, oððe to hlafordsearwe oððe to ængum<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Af_1-1.attnote.fn.11"/> unryhtum fultume, þæt is þonne ryhtre to áleoganne<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_1-1.attnote.fn.12"/> þonne to gelæstanne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="284" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hwa to hwæðrum þissa genied sie on woh, oððe to hlafordsearwe oððe to ængum unryhtum fultume, þæt is þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> ryhtre to áleoganne þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> to gelæstanne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="47" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer [allerdings] böser Weise gezwungen worden ist zum [Versprechen] eines der beiden [Verbrechen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.de.1"/>], entweder zu Herrenverrath<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.de.2"/> oder zu irgend einer widerrechtlichen Beihilfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.de.3"/>, das ist dann richtiger zu weigern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_1-1.lnote.de.4"/>, als zu leisten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone has [indeed] been wrongfully compelled to [promise] either of the two [crimes], either treachery to his lord or any unlawful assistance, it is then more right to refuse that than to perform it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="63" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone is wrongfully constrained to promise either of these: to betray his lord or to render aid in an unlawful undertaking, then it is better to be false [to the promise] than to perform it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="410" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone is wrongfully compelled to either of these, [to promise] treachery against his lord or any illegal aid, then it is better to leave it unfulfilled than to perform it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="285" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone is wrongfully forced to either of these things – either to treason against one’s lord or to any unlawful assistance – then it is better to repudiate [the oath] than to perform it</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="271"><ref target="clause:Af_El-to-49-7">Af El 49.7</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.48" n="48" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ðerum [-ðeru <hi rend="italic">So</hi>] þissum genyd [genydde <hi rend="italic">So</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Ld So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ðerum [-ðeru So] þissum genyd [genydde So] Ld So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.49" n="49" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.50" n="50" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-desyrwe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-desyrwe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.51" n="51" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ænig. <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ænig. So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.52" n="52" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rih. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rih. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a prodicione <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a prodicione T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ment. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ment. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Herrenverrat 4; Beihilfe 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Herrenverrat 4; Beihilfe 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> El 49, 7¹⁷</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> El 49, 7¹⁷</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bedas <hi rend="italic">cooperator</hi> wird Agsä. übs. <hi rend="italic">fultumend; Hist. eccl.</hi> III 30</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Bede’s <hi rend="italic">cooperator</hi> is rendered in Anglo-Saxon by <hi rend="italic">fultumend; Hist. eccl.</hi> III 30</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_1-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aleogan</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>) [Versprechen] ‘brechen, to be false to’, oft, auch aus Ælfred, belegt bei Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> neuengl. <hi rend="italic">to belie</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">aleogan</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>) [a promise] ‘to break, to be false to’, often attested, including from Ælfred, in Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Modern English <hi rend="italic">to belie</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_1-1.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><label>sie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">to hwæðerum þisra genyd sy</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_1-1.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><label>ængum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ænigum</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_1-1.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><label>áleoganne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">aleogenne</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
